Read `CLAUDE.md` at the repo root before changing code. Key rules:

- Two modes, one codebase: `DATA_MODE=demo` (seed, role switcher, demo clock) and `DATA_MODE=real`
  (admin uploads via `backend/app/ingest`, Firebase sign-in, Cloud SQL). Real figures only enter through uploads.
- Demand math, flags and lead-rule evaluation are mirrored in Python (`backend/app/services/demand_math.py`,
 `flags.py`, `lead_rules.py`) and TypeScript (`packages/web/src/lib/demandMath.ts`, `flags.ts`, `leadRules.ts`).
 Change both and regenerate the golden cases.
- Jev (decisions) and Gemini (prose) are only reached through `backend/app/ai/decision_provider.py`, which
  honours the `DecisionPolicy` (Jev is off in real mode until the admin setting allows it).
- Every data route depends on `app/middleware/auth.get_current_user`; submissions check the rep's scopes.
- Figures are keyed by country + micro-segment; the cube is built per (country, mega-segment).
- Postgres identifiers must stay under 63 characters. Schema changes go through Alembic and `alembic check`.
- Frontend: TanStack Query hooks for data, no network calls on the keystroke path, strict TS.
